    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0688" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg668"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 5, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Referring to your note of the 11th of
                    last month, relative to the appeal in the case of the steamer Pearl, I have the
                    honor to inform your lordship, <pb facs="0689" n="669" xml:id="pg669"/> in
                    reply, that the Attorney General will examine the facts, with a view to enable
                    me to decide upon the propriety of dismissing the appeal, as soon as he shall
                    have received the proper record.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, my lord, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons.</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
